Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: keep Slot 1 on CLKDIV byte 0 (7.2 single-slot port)

On the ESP32-P4 CLKSRC stays zero, so physical Slot 1 still reads divider 0.
Writing the requested divider to the whole CLKDIV register is fine on a
single-slot upstream driver, but keep the read-modify-write so only byte 0
is updated -- identical end state to the 6.18 series (0007 slot-shifted
block + this revert), expressed directly on the 7.2 code.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -1165,9 +1165,14 @@
 		/* inform CIU */
 		mci_send_cmd(host, sdmmc_cmd_bits, 0);
 
-		/* set clock to desired speed */
-		mci_writel(host, CLKDIV, div);
+		/*
+		 * CLKSRC remains zero, so physical Slot 1 also selects divider 0.
+		 * Updating divider 1 leaves the card at the bypass clock and makes
+		 * the existing command/data timeout calculations inconsistent.
+		 */
+		mci_writel(host, CLKDIV,
+			   (mci_readl(host, CLKDIV) & ~0xffu) | (div & 0xffu));
 
 		/* inform CIU */
 		mci_send_cmd(host, sdmmc_cmd_bits, 0);
